# DBG-DRAW: the gameplay debug drawing (Core/DebugDraw.hpp, UE DrawDebugHelpers) over the TONEMAPPED final image
# (SceneRenderer::AddFrameDebugDraw, UE's editor-primitives composite), depth-tested against the scene; a point is a
# square of fixed screen size (UE DrawDebugPoint). DBG_DebugDraw.desce runs DebugDrawDemo.lua: at the start of Play
# it draws, for 2 s of world time, a red line through the cube, a green box around it, a blue sphere half sunk into
# the ground, a thick yellow arrow, the label "DebugDraw: 2 s" and 12-pixel points pure red / green / blue (a fourth,
# magenta, at the cube's centre - hidden by the cube).
Проект Projects/Desert/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/DBG_DebugDraw.desce
Дано run View "View mode: Lit"
Когда run Action "Play"
Когда advance 0.5
Тогда-вид 1_draw the line, box, sphere, arrow, label and three point squares (same size on screen) are drawn in their exact given colours - pure red, green and blue squares, not exposure-dimmed or tonemapped; the line's part inside the cube, the sphere's lower half under the ground and the magenta point at the cube's centre are hidden by the depth test; the label reads "DebugDraw: 2 s"; 0 VUID in editor.log
Когда advance 1.5
Когда advance 1.0
Тогда-вид 2_expired at 3 s every debug item (lines, box, sphere, arrow, label, points) is gone - only the scene; editor.log has 0 error lines
